{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473741-vitae-from-werewolves-and-abominations","id":1473741,"title":"Vitae from Werewolves and Abominations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-01T03:40:30-08:00","id":1473741,"title":"Vitae from Werewolves and Abominations","content":"For the core book, Lupine Vitae is powerful and makes Frenzy harder to resist.<br /> <br /> Two quick questions.<br /> <br /> 1) If a vampire drinks lupine blood - therefore converting it into Vitae - than gives some of this Vitae to a Ghoul or another vampire, it's just common vitae or it retains lupine blood properties?<br /> <br /> 2) The blood of an Abomination is different from normal vampiric Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T07:47:28-08:00","id":1473750,"title":"","content":"A vampire is not a machine for pumping, converting, or distilling blood, (i.e. they're not fire engines/cement trucks/or other similar devices filled with blood), so the answer to mechanistic questions like this really should be obvious: no<br /> <br /> Abominations are not covered by the V20 rules (afaik) so you'd have to decide for yourself. Mixing and matching different sets of the rules is always a house rule so it's entirely up to the ST and the players in any campaign which makes it kind of pointless to ask in a forum, unless you make the question about how people have played this in their campaigns.<br /> <br /> Lastly, it's much more helpful to mention which version of the rules you are asking about. e.g. V20, p380 'Dangerous Draughts' details the advantages and disadvantages of drinking werewolf blood, although it is also mentioned on p270 in passing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T11:36:06-08:00","id":1473763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473741-vitae-from-werewolves-and-abominations#post1473741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the core book, Lupine Vitae is powerful and makes Frenzy harder to resist.<br /> <br /> Two quick questions.<br /> <br /> 1) If a vampire drinks lupine blood - therefore converting it into Vitae - than gives some of this Vitae to a Ghoul or another vampire, it's just common vitae or it retains lupine blood properties?<br /> <br /> 2) The blood of an Abomination is different from normal vampiric Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that consuming Lupine blood would trigger a frenzy that needs to be fought (unless the vampire practices a Path of Enlightenment/Road that encourages riding the frenzy) &amp; MAYBE it would give said vampire a temporary boost in physical stats depending upon the Rank of the Lupine. Abominations are all up to you but I would have the consumption of such blood come with the danger of developing a derangement or two depending upon the Abomination's Generation/former Rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T08:28:39-08:00","id":1473829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473741-vitae-from-werewolves-and-abominations?p=1473750#post1473750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A vampire is not a machine for pumping, converting, or distilling blood, (i.e. they're not fire engines/cement trucks/or other similar devices filled with blood)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An extract from the story I'm writing:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i><b> The ancient Methuselah lied staked and chained in the deepest level of the underground fortress, connected with a bulky machinery that feed him with the blood harvested by captive werewolves kept bind and comatose in large vats filled by obnoxious solutions.<br /> The werewolf-based Vitae was being slowly extracted from the vampire's undead heart by central vascular catheter and mixed with a gelatine-based alchemical carrier, then it slowly solidified into into dark crystals at extremely low temperatures.<br /> It was a time-demanding process that requires supervision and great amount of energy, provided by atomic batteries. Once the crystals formed, they looked like tiny shining black diamonds.<br /> These Vitae gems contained an unbelievable amount of mystical power.<br /> <br /> The centuries-old ghoul alchemist indulged in a satisfied chuckle, wondering if Caine's own blood was so much different from the alchemical wonder he concocted.</b></i></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ( crimson blood text for pathos effect )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 02-02-2022, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T08:25:54-08:00","id":1474078,"title":"","content":"Drink from a vampire and you're just drinking their vitae, I'd rule, regardless of what diet they're on.<br /> <br /> I'd also rule that abomination vitae is definitely just regular old vampire vitae. The creature lost the vital force that made it a fera when it was embraced.<br /> <br /> I freely admit that I'm going with the guesses that suit me in the absence of hard and fast rules to the contrary.<br /> <br /> It should also be noted that there's nothing stopping a mad scientist character from doing some truly horrible experiments in the hopes of making something happen here. They'd make for a good gothic horror antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 02-06-2022, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T11:28:44-08:00","id":1474086,"title":"","content":"There are two sources for Abominations in V20, and 0 in V5 as of the writing of this comment. In <i><b>The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</b></i>, pages 139 to 141, presents Abominations as mad caitiffs who only know violence and crave the sweet release of final death. If we look at Werewolf for a bit, the book <b><i>Changing Breeds</i></b>, pages 224 to 225, presents these creatures are beasts as walking tragedies waiting to fall to the wyrm. With all that out of the way let's answer the questions with the information we have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473741-vitae-from-werewolves-and-abominations#post1473741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) If a vampire drinks lupine blood - therefore converting it into Vitae - than gives some of this Vitae to a Ghoul or another vampire, it's just common vitae or it retains lupine blood properties?</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 page 380 implies that vitae is not a pure 1 to 1 conversion, with talk of the blood being in their system. Based on RAW, one could argue that vitae made from werewolf blood holds a lot of the same properties in V20, albeit requiring twice the amount for the same effect. This wording continues in V5 on page 376, giving credit to the idea that a vampire may get the same effect of werewolf blood if they drink from a vampire who recently drank said blood, even if never explicitly stated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473741-vitae-from-werewolves-and-abominations#post1473741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The blood of an Abomination is different from normal vampiric Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the answer to the earlier question as a precedent, and the rules for abominations in V20 and W20, I can safely say that by RAW there is no difference. Vitae is made from the stolen blood of one's victims and may carry trace amounts of the victims' properties until used. Abominations cannot produce their own vitae, just like every other vampire, so I can safely say there is no difference RAW. <i><b>In game/in story is completely different btw, there is no chance in hell that Abomination vitae don't have some kinda of property to it.</b></i><br /> <br /> Ultimately this is all speculation laced with observations and interpretations. As always, story trumps rules in this situation. All I am attempting to do is provide evidence for what I have gathered.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T11:28:44-08:00","id":1474087,"title":"","content":"IDK why it double posted. Hopefully this edit works until this post can be deleted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Please Delete! Post uploaded twice for some reason. 02-06-2022, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}